## ENERGY SAVING MODE

This machine is equipped with an energy saving feature. The machine will automatically enter power off mode after 9 minutes. To turn the machine on, either press the Espresso or Lungo button.

To turn the machine off before automatic Power Off mode, press both the Espresso and Lungo button simultaneously.
<PIC:Manual07_4>
{{image description: Blue line icon showing a finger pressing one of two cup buttons on the coffee machine control panel.}}


<PIC:Manual07_5>
{{image description: Blue line icon showing two fingers pressing both cup buttons at the same time.}}

### To change this setting

1. With machine turned off, press and hold the Espresso button for 3 seconds.

2. The Espresso button will blink to indicate the current setting.
<PIC:Manual07_6>
{{image description: Blue line icon showing a finger pressing the small cup, Espresso, button.}}


3. To change this setting, press the Espresso button: one time for power off mode after 9 minutes, one more time for power off mode after 30 minutes, one more time to deactivate.
<PIC:Manual07_7>
{{image description: Blue icon of a cup button with radiating lines, indicating the button is blinking or illuminated.}}


4. To exit the energy saving mode, press the Lungo button for 3 seconds.
<PIC:Manual07_8>
{{image description: Blue line icon showing a finger pressing one cup button, with the button centered above a horizontal line.}}


<PIC:Manual07_9>
{{image description: Blue line icon showing a finger pressing the small cup button inside a framed instruction panel.}}

## COFFEE PREPARATION

1. Rinse then fill the water tank with drinkable water.

2. Press the Espresso or Lungo button to activate the machine.
<PIC:Manual07_17>
{{image description: Illustration of water being poured from a bottle into a glass or water container for rinsing or filling.}}


Blinking lights: heating up (25 seconds)
Steady lights: ready
<PIC:Manual07_18>
{{image description: Blue line icon showing a finger pressing two cup buttons on the machine control panel.}}

3. Lift the lever completely and insert a capsule. CAUTION: never lift lever during operation and refer to the important safeguards to avoid possible harm when operating the appliance. NOTE: during heat up, you can press either coffee button while blinking. The coffee will then flow automatically when the machine is ready.
<PIC:Manual07_19>
{{image description: Panel showing two coffee button icons blinking above a line and two steady button icons below it, indicating heating or ready light states.}}


4. Close the lever and place a cup under the coffee outlet.
<PIC:Manual07_20>
{{image description: Close-up of the coffee machine lever with a capsule shown being dropped into the capsule opening, indicated by blue arrows.}}


5. Press the Espresso (40 ml / 1.35 oz) or the Lungo (110 ml / 3.7 oz) button to start. Preparation will stop automatically. To stop the coffee flow manually or add more coffee, press again.
<PIC:Manual07_21>
{{image description: Close-up of a cup being placed on the drip grid under the coffee outlet, with a blue arrow pointing inward.}}


6. Remove the cup. Lift and close the lever to eject the capsule into the used capsule container.
<PIC:Manual07_22>
{{image description: Blue line icon showing a finger pressing the two coffee buttons inside a framed instruction panel.}}


<PIC:Manual07_23>
{{image description: Close-up of the machine lever or capsule holder being closed downward, indicated by blue curved arrows.}}

## TROUBLESHOOTING

<PIC:Manual07_49>
{{image description: Bilingual English and French troubleshooting table for an espresso machine. The English section lists problems such as no light indicator, no coffee or no water, coffee comes out very slowly, coffee is not hot enough, capsule area is leaking, irregular blinking, and no coffee with only water running out. Recommended actions include checking mains plug, voltage and fuse, filling the water tank with warm water for first use, filling the water tank, descaling if necessary, preheating the cup, positioning the capsule correctly, sending the appliance for repair, or calling the Nespresso Club.}}

